	{
		"title": "A ClientHello, then the client shuts down its write half",
		"kind": "closed",
		"request": "A complete ClientHello, immediately followed by a TCP FIN on the client's write half. No Finished will ever arrive.",
		"request_hex": "",
		"response": "The server may send its whole flight anyway, and then closes. Either way the process survives and the next connection is accepted.",
		"response_hex": "",
		"note": "read() == 0 means the peer will send nothing more. Free that connection's state and return to accept(); it is not an error condition.",
