	{
		"title": "An abandoned handshake",
		"kind": "text",
		"request": "The client sends a ClientHello, reads the ServerHello, and then simply stops — no Finished, no close_notify, the socket left open.",
		"request_hex": "",
		"response": "Nothing, until the server's own timeout. What matters is that the server is still accepting new connections while it waits.",
		"response_hex": "",
		"note": "This is what a port scanner and a flaky mobile client both look like. A server that blocks its accept loop on one half-finished handshake is trivially denied service by a single connection.",
